#: ../../source/api_Client.md:1
msgid "Class: Client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:3
msgid "Extends: `undici.Dispatcher`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:5
msgid ""
"A basic HTTP/1.1 client, mapped on top a single TCP/TLS connection. "
"Pipelining is disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:7
msgid "Requests are not guaranteed to be dispatched in order of invocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:9
msgid "`new Client(url[, options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:11
msgid "Arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:13
msgid ""
"**url** `URL | string` - Should only include the **protocol, hostname, "
"and port**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:14
msgid "**options** `ClientOptions` (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:16
msgid "Returns: `Client`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:18
msgid "Parameter: `ClientOptions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:20
msgid ""
"**bodyTimeout** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `300e3` - The "
"timeout after which a request will time out, in milliseconds. Monitors "
"time between receiving body data. Use `0` to disable it entirely. "
"Defaults to 300 seconds. Please note the `timeout` will be reset if you "
"keep writing data to the socket everytime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:21
msgid ""
"**headersTimeout** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `300e3` - The "
"amount of time, in milliseconds, the parser will wait to receive the "
"complete HTTP headers while not sending the request. Defaults to 300 "
"seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:22
msgid ""
"**keepAliveMaxTimeout** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `600e3` - "
"The maximum allowed `keepAliveTimeout`, in milliseconds, when overridden "
"by *keep-alive* hints from the server. Defaults to 10 minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:23
msgid ""
"**keepAliveTimeout** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `4e3` - The "
"timeout, in milliseconds, after which a socket without active requests "
"will time out. Monitors time between activity on a connected socket. This"
" value may be overridden by *keep-alive* hints from the server. See [MDN:"
" HTTP - Headers - Keep-Alive directives](https://developer.mozilla.org"
"/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Keep-Alive#directives) for more details. "
"Defaults to 4 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:24
msgid ""
"**keepAliveTimeoutThreshold** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `2e3`"
" - A number of milliseconds subtracted from server *keep-alive* hints "
"when overriding `keepAliveTimeout` to account for timing inaccuracies "
"caused by e.g. transport latency. Defaults to 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:25
msgid ""
"**maxHeaderSize** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `--max-http-"
"header-size` or `16384` - The maximum length of request headers in bytes."
" Defaults to Node.js' --max-http-header-size or 16KiB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:26
msgid ""
"**maxResponseSize** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `-1` - The "
"maximum length of response body in bytes. Set to `-1` to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:27
msgid ""
"**pipelining** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `1` - The amount of "
"concurrent requests to be sent over the single TCP/TLS connection "
"according to "
"[RFC7230](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7230#section-6.3.2). Carefully "
"consider your workload and environment before enabling concurrent "
"requests as pipelining may reduce performance if used incorrectly. "
"Pipelining is sensitive to network stack settings as well as head of line"
" blocking caused by e.g. long running requests. Set to `0` to disable "
"keep-alive connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:28
msgid ""
"**connect** `ConnectOptions | Function | null` (optional) - Default: "
"`null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:29
msgid ""
"**strictContentLength** `Boolean` (optional) - Default: `true` - Whether "
"to treat request content length mismatches as errors. If true, an error "
"is thrown when the request content-length header doesn't match the length"
" of the request body. **Security Warning:** Disabling this option can "
"expose your application to HTTP Request Smuggling attacks, where "
"mismatched content-length headers cause servers and proxies to interpret "
"request boundaries differently. This can lead to cache poisoning, "
"credential hijacking, and bypassing security controls. Only disable this "
"in controlled environments where you fully trust the request source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:30
msgid ""
"**autoSelectFamily**: `boolean` (optional) - Default: depends on local "
"Node version, on Node 18.13.0 and above is `false`. Enables a family "
"autodetection algorithm that loosely implements section 5 of [RFC "
"8305](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8305#section-5). See "
"[here](https://nodejs.org/api/net.html#socketconnectoptions-"
"connectlistener) for more details. This option is ignored if not "
"supported by the current Node version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:31
msgid ""
"**autoSelectFamilyAttemptTimeout**: `number` - Default: depends on local "
"Node version, on Node 18.13.0 and above is `250`. The amount of time in "
"milliseconds to wait for a connection attempt to finish before trying the"
" next address when using the `autoSelectFamily` option. See "
"[here](https://nodejs.org/api/net.html#socketconnectoptions-"
"connectlistener) for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:32
msgid ""
"**allowH2**: `boolean` - Default: `false`. Enables support for H2 if the "
"server has assigned bigger priority to it through ALPN negotiation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:33
msgid ""
"**useH2c**: `boolean` - Default: `false`. Enforces h2c for non-https "
"connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:34
msgid ""
"**maxConcurrentStreams**: `number` - Default: `100`. Dictates the maximum"
" number of concurrent streams for a single H2 session. It can be "
"overridden by a SETTINGS remote frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:35
msgid ""
"**initialWindowSize**: `number` (optional) - Default: `262144` (256KB). "
"Sets the HTTP/2 stream-level flow-control window size "
"(SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE). Must be a positive integer greater than "
"0. This default is higher than Node.js core's default (65535 bytes) to "
"improve throughput, Node's choice is very conservative for current high-"
"bandwith networks. See [RFC 7540 Section "
"6.9.2](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7540#section-6.9.2) for "
"more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:36
msgid ""
"**connectionWindowSize**: `number` (optional) - Default `524288` (512KB)."
" Sets the HTTP/2 connection-level flow-control window size using "
"`ClientHttp2Session.setLocalWindowSize()`. Must be a positive integer "
"greater than 0. This provides better flow control for the entire "
"connection across multiple streams. See [Node.js HTTP/2 "
"documentation](https://nodejs.org/api/http2.html#clienthttp2sessionsetlocalwindowsize)"
" for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:37
msgid ""
"**pingInterval**: `number` - Default: `60e3`. The time interval in "
"milliseconds between PING frames sent to the server. Set to `0` to "
"disable PING frames. This is only applicable for HTTP/2 connections. This"
" will emit a `ping` event on the client with the duration of the ping in "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:39
msgid "**Notes about HTTP/2**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:40
msgid "It only works under TLS connections. h2c is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:41
msgid ""
"The server must support HTTP/2 and choose it as the protocol during the "
"ALPN negotiation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:42
msgid "The server must not have a bigger priority for HTTP/1.1 than HTTP/2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:43
msgid ""
"Pseudo headers are automatically attached to the request. If you try to "
"set them, they will be overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:44
msgid "The `:path` header is automatically set to the request path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:45
msgid "The `:method` header is automatically set to the request method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:46
msgid "The `:scheme` header is automatically set to the request scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:47
msgid "The `:authority` header is automatically set to the request `host[:port]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:48
msgid "`PUSH` frames are yet not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:50
msgid "Parameter: `ConnectOptions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:52
msgid ""
"Every Tls option, see "
"[here](https://nodejs.org/api/tls.html#tls_tls_connect_options_callback)."
" Furthermore, the following options can be passed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:55
msgid ""
"**socketPath** `string | null` (optional) - Default: `null` - An IPC "
"endpoint, either Unix domain socket or Windows named pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:56
msgid ""
"**maxCachedSessions** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `100` - "
"Maximum number of TLS cached sessions. Use 0 to disable TLS session "
"caching. Default: 100."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:57
msgid "**timeout** `number | null` (optional) -  In milliseconds, Default `10e3`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:58
msgid "**servername** `string | null` (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:59
msgid ""
"**keepAlive** `boolean | null` (optional) - Default: `true` - TCP keep-"
"alive enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Client.md:60
msgid ""
"**keepAliveInitialDelay** `number | null` (optional) - Default: `60000` -"
" TCP keep-alive interval for the socket in milliseconds"
msgstr ""

